# Raw downloaded archives (large). Parquet parsed output is the committed/portable artifact.
data/raw/**/*.lzh
# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.uv/
.pytest_cache/
# Reports images can be large; keep markdown, ignore heavy binaries if needed
# (kept tracked for now)
# Derived from data/raw, which the downloader rebuilds in ~2.4h. Committing a
# ~100MB entries.parquet to carry data that regenerates itself is the wrong
# trade; data/odds/*.jsonl is committed precisely because it does NOT regenerate
# (the site only retains recent seasons' odds).
data/parquet/*.parquet

# Odds: the parquet IS committed and the JSONL is not.
#
# Neither regenerates - the site only retains recent seasons - so one of them
# must be kept, and refetching a season costs ~15 hours. The parquet holds the
# same prices at a fifth the size (9.5MB vs 50MB) and done_from_parquet rebuilds
# the resume ledger from it, so the JSONL stays local as the crash-safe append
# target during a run.
data/odds/*.jsonl
